  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "A reliable and desirable coral-bark maple with leaves similar to those of the popular 'Sango kaku', 'Eddisbury' does not grow as tall and its deeper bright red shoots and leafstalks contrast with the green leaves throughout the growing season. The medium-sized leaves are mainly seven-lobed, the lobes ovateacuminate, fine-tipped with evenly toothed margins. The slender leafstalks are bright red. New young leaves are a lighter yellow-green with redtinged tips and edges, becoming a more uniform green in the summer. The fall colors are yellow to gold with light red overtones. This sturdy, upright plant grows vigorously when young but rarely exceeds 13 ft. (4 m) tall. Its outstanding feature is the coral-red winter shoots, the color persisting into the second and third years. The name honors the district in northwestern England where this cultivar was selected."
  },
